#!/usr/bin/env ssc
---
name: route-response
version: 0.1.0
description: A route handler that returns a Response, as std/http.ssc declares it.
---
# route-response

`std/http.ssc` declares `route(method, path, handler: Request => Response)` and a three-field
`Response(status, headers, body)`. This is the smallest program that uses that declaration.

```scalascript
[route, serve, Request, Response](std/http.ssc)

def handler(req: Request): Response =
  if req.path == "/ok" then Response(200, Map("Content-Type" -> "text/plain"), "ok")
  else Response(404, Map("Content-Type" -> "text/plain"), "missing")

def main(): Unit =
  route("GET", "/ok", req => handler(req))
  println("registered")
```
